      <li class="check" data-basics-card>
        <span class="check-box" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><path d="M6 22 L16 32 L36 4" /></svg></span>
        <h3>Best time to visit Sri Lanka</h3>
        <p>December to April is dry on the west and south coasts, in Colombo, Kandy and the hill country. May to September suits the east coast, including Trincomalee and Arugam Bay.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="check" data-basics-card>
        <span class="check-box" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><path d="M6 22 L16 32 L36 4" /></svg></span>
        <h3>Visa and ETA</h3>
        <p>Most visitors need an Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) before travelling; some nationalities can enter visa-free. Check your passport on the official site, <a href="https://www.eta.gov.lk/" class="underline underline-offset-4" rel="noopener">eta.gov.lk</a>.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="check" data-basics-card>
        <span class="check-box" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><path d="M6 22 L16 32 L36 4" /></svg></span>
        <h3>When to book</h3>
        <p>For December to March, book two to three months ahead, as good hotels and reserved train seats sell out. Outside peak season a tour can often be arranged within a few days.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
